  "step_3": "The decision reason requires attention to outcomes with less than 20% probability and an adjustment of their weights. Only Lottery A has such an outcome (10% chance of 0€). However, the individual does not mention this low-probability event at all; instead, they focus on the 90% chance of winning in A and the comparative riskiness of B. The justification is based on preferring a high-probability gain, not on overweighting small-probability events. There is no evidence that the individual gave extra consideration to the 10% failure chance in A, nor did they discuss distorting probabilities in a way consistent with the reason. The information considered (high-probability wins) and the justification (greater certainty) do not align with the reason’s focus on small-probability weighting. Therefore, it is unlikely the individual used this specific decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
